OL,3,GNEWSA#100,000 boost for community
OL,4,Aeco-friendly projects
OL,5,
OL,6,FA share of #100,000 is being offered to
OL,7,Fcommunity groups and young people to be
OL,8,Fused for environmentally-friendly
OL,9,Fprojects.
OL,11,FGroups can apply for up to #5,000 from
OL,12,Fthe grant, which is being given out by
OL,13,Fthe West Midlands Combined Authority
OL,14,F(WMCA) as part of its Circular Economy
OL,15,FCall to Action Fund.
OL,17,FThe authority has teamed up with
OL,18,FBloomberg Philanthropies to set up a
OL,19,Fseparate pot for 15 to 24-year-olds,
OL,20,Fthe Youth Climate Action Fund, which
OL,21,Foffers grants of up to #2,500.
OL,23,APub: 14-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
